140
00:08:52,280 --> 00:08:54,260
Let the duel continue.

141
00:08:57,000 --> 00:09:03,517
Oh, I forgot to mention that you lose 500
life points every time my turn begins.

142
00:09:03,600 --> 00:09:09,080
Thanks to the special ability of my
Nightmare Wheel Trap Card. Whatever.

143
00:09:09,660 --> 00:09:14,300
And of course, my Legendary
Fiend gained 700 attack points.

144
00:09:16,200 --> 00:09:18,800
Now it's time to feel his wrath.

145
00:09:19,160 --> 00:09:22,360
Legendary Fiend, attack
his little wing guard.

146
00:09:24,600 --> 00:09:25,620
Oh, no.

147
00:09:26,040 --> 00:09:27,540
And there's more.

148
00:09:27,900 --> 00:09:29,040
What's going on?

149
00:09:29,320 --> 00:09:32,677
Every time one of your
monsters goes to the graveyard,

150
00:09:32,760 --> 00:09:36,280
Coffin' Cellar takes
300 of your life points.

151
00:09:37,100 --> 00:09:40,000
Next, I'll place one card face down

152
00:09:41,060 --> 00:09:42,320
and end my turn.

153
00:09:43,320 --> 00:09:44,150
Finally.

154
00:09:44,620 --> 00:09:48,080
Make your move, although it's hopeless.

155
00:09:48,480 --> 00:09:53,280
As soon as I unleash my
Malevolent Catastrophe trap card,

156
00:09:53,580 --> 00:09:55,420
that fool will be devastated.

157
00:09:55,840 --> 00:10:00,757
For once it's activated, every monster
on the field will go to the graveyard.

158
00:10:00,840 --> 00:10:04,697
but that's not all thanks
to my coffin seller

159
00:10:04,780 --> 00:10:08,577
trap card he'll lose
300 life coins for every

160
00:10:08,660 --> 00:10:11,657
creature that's destroyed
then I'll wipe out the

161
00:10:11,740 --> 00:10:14,780
rest of his life coins
with my legendary fiend

162
00:10:15,520 --> 00:10:18,777
this doesn't look good
not from Joey at least

163
00:10:18,860 --> 00:10:22,417
well I must say I'm not surprised time for

164
00:10:22,500 --> 00:10:27,177
my comeback it goes Maric's trap cards are

165
00:10:27,260 --> 00:10:29,848
doing me in each one
is worse than the next.

166
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:34,235
I guess, like Yugi says, I gotta put
my faith in the heart of the cards.

167
00:10:34,980 --> 00:10:36,517
Why are you hesitating?

168
00:10:36,600 --> 00:10:41,140
Perhaps you finally realize that
there's no way you can win this duel.

169
00:10:41,380 --> 00:10:42,210
Trust

170
00:10:43,440 --> 00:10:47,357
me, before long you'll be trapped
in the Shadow Realm, fool.

171
00:10:47,440 --> 00:10:48,460
We'll see.

172
00:10:48,800 --> 00:10:50,620
Yes, we'll see how long

173
00:10:53,140 --> 00:10:56,157
you last before I banish
you into the darkness.

174
00:10:56,240 --> 00:10:58,800
It's my move, Merrick, and you're going

175
00:11:01,100 --> 00:11:03,917
The card I'm holding in
my hand right now is going

176
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:07,420
to put an end to your entire
dueling strategy. You lie!

177
00:11:07,620 --> 00:11:08,540
I'm afraid not.

178
00:11:08,860 --> 00:11:10,380
Check it out, Marek.

179
00:11:10,500 --> 00:11:13,340
It's a card I like to call... Question!

180
00:11:14,620 --> 00:11:15,580
Huh? Question?

181
00:11:16,060 --> 00:11:18,557
This bad boy forces you
to guess which one of

182
00:11:18,640 --> 00:11:21,287
my monsters is at the
bottom of my graveyard.

183
00:11:21,540 --> 00:11:22,370
What?

184
00:11:22,453 --> 00:11:25,617
Now, if you guess right, that
monster is out of the game for good.

185
00:11:25,700 --> 00:11:27,160
But if you mess up,

186
00:11:27,340 --> 00:11:31,811
it gets summoned to the field and I can
use it to take control of this tool.

187
00:11:32,360 --> 00:11:33,460
Come on.

188
00:11:33,760 --> 00:11:34,642
Are you scared?

189
00:11:35,060 --> 00:11:37,860
Just take a guess, tough guy. I'm waiting.

190
00:11:38,460 --> 00:11:41,957
The worst that could happen is
you guess wrong and I crush you.

191
00:11:42,040 --> 00:11:43,780
I must remember.

192
00:11:44,400 --> 00:11:47,480
Which of his monsters did I destroy first?

193
00:11:48,280 --> 00:11:51,357
Perhaps it was that
alligator sword of his.

194
00:11:51,440 --> 00:11:55,720
No, that card was already
removed from his graveyard.

195
00:11:56,600 --> 00:12:01,500
I've destroyed so many of Joey's monsters,
I can't remember which one was first.

196
00:12:02,080 --> 00:12:06,860
Perhaps it was one of the cards my
Help-O-Emma destroyed, but which one?

197
00:12:07,020 --> 00:12:09,280
You're in trouble. Want to know why?

198
00:12:09,500 --> 00:12:10,657
Well, I'll tell you.

199
00:12:10,740 --> 00:12:16,000
The first card that went to my graveyard
was chosen randomly by your Help-O-Emma.

200
00:12:16,340 --> 00:12:17,577
So guess what?

201
00:12:17,660 --> 00:12:21,425
There's no way you can remember
the first monster you destroyed,

202
00:12:21,540 --> 00:12:23,834
because you never saw which one it was.

203
00:12:24,380 --> 00:12:26,000
How much time left, folks?

204
00:12:26,360 --> 00:12:27,440
Five seconds?

205
00:12:29,420 --> 00:12:33,700
Five, four, three, two, one. Time's up.

206
00:12:34,460 --> 00:12:35,940
Oh, I'm sorry.

207
00:12:36,400 --> 00:12:39,237
Stunned silence was not the
answer we were looking for.

208
00:12:39,320 --> 00:12:41,837
The joke will be on him
when my catastrophic

209
00:12:41,920 --> 00:12:45,137
trap car destroys every
monster on the field.

210
00:12:45,220 --> 00:12:47,120
Oh, well, guess what?

211
00:12:47,340 --> 00:12:51,600
You guessed wrong, so I
get to summon this! Jinzo!

212
00:12:55,520 --> 00:12:56,350
Ah!

213
00:12:56,480 --> 00:12:57,560
Not Jinzo!

214
00:12:57,880 --> 00:12:58,917
That's right, pal.

215
00:12:59,000 --> 00:13:00,917
And I bet you know what that means.

216
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:04,882
It's time to say goodbye to every
trap card you have on the field.

217
00:13:05,040 --> 00:13:06,680
Jinzo, strut your stuff!

218
00:13:12,900 --> 00:13:16,660
I just turned your entire game
plan completely upside down,

219
00:13:16,820 --> 00:13:18,637
Merrick, and it serves you right.

220
00:13:18,720 --> 00:13:21,820
Nice one, man. It's all you. Well done.

221
00:13:22,100 --> 00:13:25,865
Without the use of his trap cards,
Merrick needs a new strategy.

222
00:13:26,180 --> 00:13:27,980
All right. Go.

223
00:13:28,640 --> 00:13:30,228
What's the matter, Merrick?

224
00:13:30,320 --> 00:13:31,320
In a bad mood?

225
00:13:31,740 --> 00:13:34,917
I'd be mad too if I were
on the other side of Jinzo.

226
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:37,920
He's the first monster
I won at Battle City.

227
00:13:38,200 --> 00:13:40,620
Here, my Jinzo and my Locator card.

228
00:13:40,960 --> 00:13:42,160
You deserve them.

229
00:13:43,020 --> 00:13:43,850
Thanks.

230
00:13:44,340 --> 00:13:46,940
Look, I'm sorry about that cheating thing.

231
00:13:47,660 --> 00:13:48,740
Ah, no worries.

232
00:13:49,620 --> 00:13:51,117
You beat me fair and square.

233
00:13:51,200 --> 00:13:54,140
And next time we duel,
I'm playing totally legit.

234
00:13:54,560 --> 00:13:55,560
No more cheating.

235
00:13:56,080 --> 00:13:57,440
I'll hold you to that.

236
00:13:57,820 --> 00:14:00,349
Until then, smell you
later, Robo-Brothers.

237
00:14:01,020 --> 00:14:03,500
You know, we're a lot alike, Esper.

238
00:14:04,900 --> 00:14:08,820
You've got your brothers, and
I've got my sister and my pals,

239
00:14:09,060 --> 00:14:12,037
and we're all there to support
each other when we need it.

240
00:14:12,120 --> 00:14:14,920
As long as we got that, nobody loses.

241
00:14:15,680 --> 00:14:18,920
I wasn't alone back then,
and I'm not alone now.

242
00:14:19,340 --> 00:14:22,980
I got my and my sister
Serenity to inspire me.

243
00:14:23,600 --> 00:14:27,180
Plus, I got the rest of the
gang down there cheering me on.

244
00:14:27,780 --> 00:14:29,280
You can do this, Joey.

245
00:14:29,600 --> 00:14:33,776
If you beat Merrick, he's out of the
tournament and the world is saved.

246
00:14:34,020 --> 00:14:35,440
All right, tough guy.

247
00:14:35,660 --> 00:14:37,366
I'm not through with you yet.

248
00:14:37,480 --> 00:14:40,877
After all, you still have a monster on
